	"bet_letter": {"name": "A Letter for Ewan", "giver": "bet", "zone": "hearth", "offer": true, "avail": "bosses:1",
		"where": "Bet Reed, at the Reeds' cottage",
		"text": "Ewan Reed went up the Stair the week before the Night, and Bet has written him a letter a night since, and has never sent one: there is nobody to send to. She has the last one, the nine-winters one, in her apron. She asks you to carry it to the Stair's foot, where the post stands, and decide there what a letter to the sky is for. Nan, who has heard all nine winters of them, says she will not read it.",
